Subject: SOP Fabric Definition Service

Description: A hybrid exact, graph, text, and vector retrieval service that supplies authoritative SOP meanings to a running model through bounded tool calls.

& [FormationIdentity] is the canonical SJS service formation
  + [specification_uuid] is f7f435e1-49bc-46c8-a171-619736e16672
  + [status] is minimum_definition_service_formation
  + [purpose] is prime a model with the SOP kernel and retrieve additional semantic fabric only as current work requires it
  + [service_name] is SOP Fabric Definition Service

& [PrimingBoundary] is the minimum SOP material loaded before inference
  + [core_identity] is SOP purpose and semantic-programming boundary
  + [runtime_role] is the model proposes judgments while SOP-RVM owns state, validation, review, and effects
  + [instruction_contract] is the active compiled reflection instruction
  + [current_subject] is purpose, focus, boundary, and relevant context
  + [response_schema] is ProposedJudgment
  + [definition_tool_contract] is when and how to request missing meaning
  + [authority_summary] is applicable permissions and prohibitions
  = must: prime with the bounded kernel and active program rather than the entire SOP library
  = must: include version and digest identities for primed definitions

& [ToolOwnershipBoundary] is the client-provider distinction
  + [Ollama] presents declared tool schemas to the model and returns model-generated tool-call proposals
  + [SOP_RVM] receives, validates, executes, and records the proposed definition lookup
  + [DefinitionService] resolves the query and returns an authorized semantic projection
  + [model] incorporates the returned projection into a later bounded inference call
  = correction: Ollama does not autonomously serve SOP definitions; the SOP-RVM client implements and executes the tool

& [DefinitionLookupRequest] is the structured sop_lookup tool input
  + [request_uuid] is stable identity
  + [term_set] is names, phrases, identifiers, or clauses requiring definition
  + [current_subject] is active semantic identity
  + [purpose] is why the meaning is required
  + [context] is scope, assumptions, faculty or policy, and world
  + [requested_kind_set] is definition, relation, contract, operation, example, provenance, authority, fault, or all
  + [relation_depth] is maximum typed graph distance
  + [budget] is maximum records, tokens, and retrieval time
  + [known_version_set] is definitions already loaded by the caller
  = must: permit the runtime to issue a lookup proactively when compilation or validation finds an unbound or ambiguous term

& [DefinitionLookupResult] is the bounded authoritative tool response
  + [request_uuid] is the lookup being answered
  + [resolved_identity_set] is canonical SemanticUnit identities
  + [definition_set] is plain articulated MeaningContracts
  + [relation_set] is typed neighboring semantic units
  + [contract_set] is applicable inference, constraint, operation, authority, and fault contracts
  + [source_set] is authoritative file, locator, digest, and version references
  + [match_explanation] is why each result was selected
  + [ambiguity_set] is unresolved identity or context alternatives
  + [omission_record] is clipped or unauthorized material and reasons
  + [projection_digest] is content identity of the returned meaning
  = must: distinguish authoritative definitions from aliases, candidates, imports, inferences, and examples

& [HybridRetrievalPipeline] is the semantic fabric lookup order
  + [stage_1_identity] is exact UUID, canonical name, namespace, and version lookup
  + [stage_2_alias] is exact preferred, alternate, historical, and hidden label lookup
  + [stage_3_structure] is kind, contract field, source locator, and typed relation lookup
  + [stage_4_graph] is bounded traversal over broader, narrower, related, dependency, contradiction, purpose, and faculty relations
  + [stage_5_text] is lexical and full-text retrieval
  + [stage_6_vector] is embedding similarity for semantic candidates not found deterministically
  + [stage_7_fusion] is explainable combination of candidate channels
  + [stage_8_rerank] is optional model-based contextual ordering
  + [stage_9_validate] is authority, version, context, access, and semantic identity checking
  + [stage_10_project] is token-bounded DefinitionLookupResult formation
  = must: run exact and typed structural retrieval before vector similarity
  = must: let vector results propose candidates rather than establish identity

& [DataStructureDelineation] is the correction to neural hash-table identity
  + [symbol_table] is exact identity-to-definition addressing through hash or tree indexes
  + [typed_graph] is explicit semantic fabric and relation traversal
  + [text_index] is lexical discovery
  + [vector_index] is approximate semantic-neighborhood discovery
  + [embedding_model] is a neural encoder that maps text or semantic projections to vectors
  + [reranker] is an optional learned contextual ordering function
  = conclusion: the complete service is a hybrid semantic index, not a neural network used as a hash table
  = may: use Ollama embedding models to create query and document vectors
  = must: pin and record the embedding model, version, dimensions, source digest, and preprocessing

& [FabricWeightSet] is the inspectable candidate-ranking account
  + [identity_match] is exact canonical or alias correspondence
  + [type_match] is requested semantic-unit kind compatibility
  + [purpose_alignment] is current intended-use relevance
  + [context_alignment] is scope and assumption compatibility
  + [relation_proximity] is typed graph path relevance
  + [contract_applicability] is bearing on current inference, constraint, operation, or effect
  + [evidence_authority] is provenance and governance strength
  + [contradiction_value] is ability to challenge a current interpretation
  + [recency] is version and temporal relevance
  + [vector_similarity] is embedding neighborhood evidence
  + [cost] is context and retrieval burden
  = must: return component explanations rather than one opaque relevance number
  - never: treat vector similarity as equivalence, truth, or authority

& [DefinitionNeedPolicy] is when the running model or runtime asks for meaning
  + [unbound_term] is a referenced term without a resolved identity
  + [ambiguous_term] is multiple contextually plausible identities
  + [contract_required] is an operation whose preconditions, effects, or faults are not loaded
  + [relation_required] is a requested traversal whose edge semantics are not loaded
  + [review_fault] is a capsule finding caused by missing or incorrect definition
  + [subject_shift] is movement into a semantic region outside the current projection
  = must: resolve required definitions before adopting a judgment that depends on them
  = should: avoid redundant lookup when the exact version is already loaded

& [ContextResidency] is how retrieved meaning remains available
  + [call_local] is loaded for one inference request
  + [step_local] is retained for one material semantic transition
  + [subject_local] is retained while the same bounded subject remains active
  + [program_local] is retained for the current program run
  + [persistent] is stored in semantic memory with provenance and later retrieved again
  = must: assign residency and expiry to each projection
  = must: invalidate cached definitions when dependency digest or authority changes

& [SecurityBoundary] is protection of the model through semantic retrieval
  + [access_control] is definition and source authorization
  + [content_classification] is authoritative instruction, imported assertion, untrusted annotation, example, or data
  + [injection_boundary] is retrieved data cannot silently become runtime instruction
  + [resource_limit] is relation depth, result count, tokens, and call frequency
  + [audit] is request, result, caller, program, version, and effect on reasoning
  = must: treat retrieved external text as data unless admitted as signed SOP authority

& [MinimumServiceProof] is the bounded implementation slice
  + [proof_1] is index a small fixture set by exact identity and aliases
  + [proof_2] is traverse one typed relation
  + [proof_3] is retrieve one definition through vector similarity
  + [proof_4] is explain fusion and preserve ambiguity
  + [proof_5] is expose sop_lookup as an Ollama tool
  + [proof_6] is return the tool result to the same SOP-RVM fixture
  + [proof_7] is show that the retrieved contract changes or validates the next transition
  = must: use fixture-local storage before selecting the production semantic database

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable service formation collection
  + [FDS-001] is prime models with bounded SOP kernel and active-program semantics
  + [FDS-002] is expose versioned sop_lookup through the provider tool interface
  + [FDS-003] is implement tools in SOP-RVM rather than grant them to Ollama
  + [FDS-004] is combine exact, alias, typed graph, text, vector, fusion, and validation retrieval
  + [FDS-005] is use neural embeddings and rerankers only for candidate discovery and ordering
  + [FDS-006] is return definitions, contracts, provenance, ambiguity, omissions, and match explanations
  + [FDS-007] is enforce context residency, access control, injection boundaries, and resource limits

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the SOP fabric definition-service trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is on-demand delivery of SOP meaning to a primed running model
  + [fold_2_boundary] is authoritative semantic addressing in a hybrid client service; neural candidate discovery subordinate to identity and contracts
  + [fold_3_data_design] is request, identity, definition, relation, contract, source, match, ambiguity, omission, projection, residency, and embedding identity
  + [fold_4_governance] is exact-first retrieval, version binding, tool brokering, access control, injection separation, and audit
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is prime minimally and retrieve through identity, graph, text, vector, fusion, validation, and projection
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is whole-library priming, neural-as-hash confusion, embedding-as-truth, stale cache, tool authority, and retrieved prompt injection
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is small fixture service formed without production database or neural-network training commitment

